.Dd November 14, 2026
.Dt RAVEN-THEME 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm raven-theme
.Nd preview, set and apply the Raven terminal palette
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm preview
.Op Fl -json
.Nm
.Cm set
.Ar name|path
.Nm
.Cm apply
.Op Fl -dry-run
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the colour front end of
.Xr raven 1 .
The default palette is
.Dq raven-violet ;
.Cm mono
and
.Cm classic
are built in.
Semantic roles are accent, muted, border, success, warning, error, info, path, number,
string and keyword.
.Pp
Colour is only emitted for a terminal and is suppressed by
.Ev NO_COLOR ,
.Ev TERM=dumb
and JSON output.
.Fl -color=always
is an explicit request for human colour.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm preview
Print the roles.
With
.Fl -json
emit one schema-1
.Dq theme
record with hex values and no escapes.
.It Cm set Ar name|path
Validate and atomically install a built-in name or a theme TOML file in the user config.
.Fl -dry-run
prints the target without writing.
.It Cm apply
Generate
.Ev LS_COLORS
and
.Ev LESS_TERMCAP_*
in
.Pa ~/.config/raven/theme.env .
An existing file is copied to
.Pa ~/.config/raven/theme.env.bak
first.
.Fl -dry-run
lists the target and backup paths without writing or starting any external tool.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev NO_COLOR
Suppress automatic colour.
.It Ev COLORTERM
.Cm truecolor
selects 24-bit output.
.It Ev TERM
A
.Cm 256color
terminal selects the 256-colour fallback.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/raven/theme.toml
System theme.
The file has a
.Ql [theme]
table with
.Va name ,
.Va variant
and an optional
.Va background ,
plus a
.Ql [colors]
table of role-to-hex values.
.It Pa ~/.config/raven/theme.toml
User theme; wins over the system file.
.It Pa ~/.config/raven/theme.env
Generated adapters.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
A configuration or write error exits 1; a usage error exits 2.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr raven 1
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD.
